From 5585ffb7c1f51182516298e0b062d8fb5d639da8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 03:06:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Import the Mos Le'Harmless cave from the 474 cache

Groundwork for cave horrors, which are where the black mask comes from - and which
cannot live anywhere until the cave they live in exists. The island's SURFACE is
already in this build as m57_46, full of Cabin Fever pirates and bankers; the cave
underneath it never was.

OSRS map squares cannot be used for this: idx5 is XTEA-encrypted and there are no keys
for that cache. The 474 cache has its keys sitting beside it, and 474 is a year after
Cabin Fever, so m58_146 / m58_147 / m59_147 decrypt and come across clean - 6,500 locs
across three squares, of which the resolver matched all but 34 back to locs this build
already owns rather than importing duplicates. 41 new models.

Two false starts worth not repeating. The squares were first picked as "surface z plus
6400", which is the right rule and gave 57_146 - a square 474 does not have. The ones
that do exist were then written off as a Construction template, because their loc ids
were looked up in the 474 config table when the jm2 stores the 377 ids the resolver had
already mapped them to; 15298 is "Table space" in 474 and something else entirely here.
Reading them the right way round gives mushrooms, boulders and swamp bubbles, which is
the cave.

Nothing is wired up yet: no npcs, no entrance from the island, no drops. rs2check 0/0,
poh_battery ALL PASS, and loc/model/map packs have no duplicate id or name.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Dc7giZ7Qnh4qy1CYPTDrmH
