From aeaf7a354deff490372bbfb0f387a29bed5d6bff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 03:29:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Import the cave horror, its animations and the witchwood
 icon

All from the 474 cache, whose models the 377 client reads without conversion. The
horror is npc 4353: two models, size 2, level 80, and a witchwood icon (obj 8923) to
go with it - inventory model plus both worn models, so it will not clip on either
gender.

THE ANIMATIONS ARE THE PART WORTH READING. An npc config names only readyanim and
walkanim; attack, block and death live in scripts the cache does not have. seqfind474
recovers the rest by working out which frame group the two known seqs sit on and
listing every other seq using it: seven, 4231-4237, all on skeleton 974, 86 frames
converted.

Stand (4231) and walk (4236) are certain - the cache says so. The other five are
INFERRED and the config says which:
  4232 attack   15 frames, last delay 3   - fast recovery, the shape of a swing
  4233 death    14 frames, last delay 20  - the longest hold, which is what a body
                                            dropping and staying down needs
  4234 block    11 frames, last delay 6   - a short flinch
  4237 screech  13 frames                 - the horror's special in OSRS
  4235 spare
Renaming two of them is a one-line fix if they look wrong in game, which is the only
way to tell: nothing here can play a 474 npc rig back.

Nothing is wired up yet - no stats, no spawns, no drops, no screech. rs2check 0/0 and
none of the seven packs touched (obj, npc, model, seq, anim, base, animset) has a
duplicate id or name.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Dc7giZ7Qnh4qy1CYPTDrmH
