From 4edc1bc47ccfc7d12d17cf8c11ccbc86f6631ca0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 03:50:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Cave horrors: the slayer task, the spawns, and the black
 mask's only source

The monster, its cave and its animations went in last commit; this is everything that makes it a
thing you can actually go and fight.

The task. ^slayer_cavehorror is 76, the next free id - no 377-era master ever assigned it, so
Chaeldar and Duradel each get a weight-8 entry and their totals move with it. Both totals are
now checked against the sum of their rows' weights, and so are the other three masters'.

The spawns. 36 horrors across the three imported squares, placed by stitching the squares into
one world grid, flooding out from the foot of the staircase, and farthest-point sampling what the
flood reached - so none of them is sealed in a pocket, and none is standing on the arrival tile.
Blocking is read properly: the map's f1 flag plus loc shapes 0-3, 9, 10 and 11. Shape 22 is
ground decor and the engine only clips it when active=yes, which nothing in either imported .loc
sets, so all of it is scenery you walk over.

The staircase. Both halves of the entrance now carry "Enter" - the cache gave the lower half no
options at all - and the cave-side landing moved to (36,30), because the tile east of the exit
that the first pass picked is clipped in the cache.

The witchwood icon is stocked at the slayer shop. It is the one thing that stops the screech, and
until now there was no way to get one: the cache gave us the item, not a source.

The dragon pickaxe goes on all three Dagannoth Kings at 1/128, on its own roll ahead of the
cascade so none of the calibrated thresholds in it shift - which is also how OSRS added it.

And rs2check learned to validate obj, npc, loc and inv NAMES, not just seqs and synths. It found
five in this drop table written from memory rather than from pack/obj.pack - bigbones,
adamant_bolts, grimy_ranarr, grimy_irit, grimy_avantoe - all plausible, all wrong, and none of
them a compile error until the packer runs. It found none anywhere else in the repo.

